course: dictionary
lesson: 10144
title: Throat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your throat is the inside of your neck, the tube that food, drink and air go down. The word can also mean the front of your neck, the part you touch when you swallow.
explain: Context helps you use the word. «Most sore throats get better by themselves in a few days with drinks and rest.» A sore throat is one that hurts, and the sentence tells you it usually gets better with drinks and rest.
explain: Throat is a noun, so it names a thing. Its plural is throats. You can also meet it in phrases such as clear your throat, which means cough a little to get rid of a tickle.
fact: Your throat is the inside of your neck, the tube that food, drink and air go down.
fact: The throat can also mean the front of the neck.
fact: Your voice box is in your throat, and a small flap stops food going down the wrong way.
fact: «Cleaning products such as bleach must never be drunk, even a little, because they burn the throat.»
fact: Tiny objects can block the throat and cause choking, so keep them away from babies.
exercise: Where is your throat? | Inside your head | Under your knees | At the end of your toes | *Inside your neck
exercise: «Most sore throats get better by themselves in a few days.» What does a sore throat feel like? | A throat that is very long | *A throat that hurts | A throat that tastes of sweets | A throat that is made of soft wood
exercise: «Cleaning products such as bleach must never be drunk, even a little, because they burn the throat.» Why must bleach never be drunk? | It tastes of lemons | It would make your hair grow | *It would burn your throat | It is too cold to swallow
test: What do food, drink and air travel down? | Your ears | *Your throat | Your elbows | Your knees
test: What can block the throat and cause choking? | Warm drinks | *Tiny objects | Clean socks | Sunshine
exam: Which is the plural of throat? | throates | throatie | throaten | *throats
